ey are wrought in God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAfter these things came Jesus and his disciples into the land of JudÃ¦a; and there he tarried with them, and baptized.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd John also was baptizing in Ã†non near to Salim, because there was much water there: and they came, and were baptized.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&For John was not yet cast into prison.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZThen there arose a question between some of John's disciples and the Jews about purifying.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©And they came unto John, and said unto him, Rabbi, he that was with thee beyond Jordan, to whom thou barest witness, behold, the same baptizeth, and all men come to him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVJohn answered and said, A man can receive nothing, except it be given him from heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Ye yourselves bear me witness, that I said, I am not the Christ, but that I am sent before him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄHe that hath the bride is the bridegroom: but the friend of the bridegroom, which standeth and heareth him, rejoiceth greatly because of the bridegroom's voice: this my joy therefore is fulfilled.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&He must increase, but I must decrease.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse$¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHe that cometh from above is above all: he that is of the earth is earthly, and speaketh of the earth: he that cometh from heaven is above all.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd what he hath seen and heard, that he testifieth; and no man receiveth his testimony.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJHe that hath received his testimony hath set to his seal that God is true.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgFor he whom God hath sent speaketh the words of God: for God giveth not the Spirit by measure unto him.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCThe Father loveth the Son, and hath given all things into his hand.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHe that believeth on the Son hath everlasting life: and he that believeth not the Son shall not see life; but the wrath of God abideth on him.¦layout ªlast_verse$